      {
        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module checks whether each extracted data column is documented in a codebook or README, and flags documented variables that never appear in the data.",
          "We examined 1 codebook/README/label source and 8 data columns across 1 file.",
          "#### Column Documentation",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## s.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"abc_99999999997\", \"abc_99999999998\", \n\"abc_99999999999\", \"id\", \"sat_1\", \"sat_2\", \"sat_3\", \"sat_4\"), \n    Documented = c(\"no\", \"no\", \"no\", \"no\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \n    \"yes\"), Label = c(NA, NA, NA, NA, \"\", \"\", \"Satisfaction with colleagues\", \n    \"\"), \"Codebook Variable\" = c(NA, NA, NA, NA, \"sat_1\", \"sat_2\", \n    \"sat_3\", \"sat_4\"), Source = c(NA, NA, NA, NA, \"codebook.csv\", \n    \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\"), Status = c(\"unlabelled\", \n    \"unlabelled\", \"unlabelled\", \"unlabelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \n    \"labelled\", \"labelled\")), row.names = c(NA, 8L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "#### Scales",
          "We detected 2 column groups (by shared abbreviation) that look like scales; 0 were matched to a named instrument from the paper text or dictionary. Groups we could not name are listed too — they are real scale-like column families whose instrument the manuscript did not identify. Identified scales are exported in the OpenScales OSD structure.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = c(\"s.csv\", \"s.csv\"), Abbrev = c(\"ABC\", \n\"SAT\"), Columns = 3:4, \"Max item\" = c(\"-Inf\", \"4\"), Scale = c(\"— not matched to a named scale —\", \n\"— not matched to a named scale —\"), Confidence = c(\"\", \"\"\n), Source = c(\"\", \"\")), row.names = c(NA, -2L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 40, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "To let this tool (and anyone reusing the data) identify these scales with **high confidence**:\n- **Name the instrument in the manuscript with its abbreviation** — e.g. \"the Breakup Distress Scale (BDS)\" — matching the column prefix.\n- **Add a codebook** giving the item wording, or state the number of items (\"a 15-item scale\").",
          "LLM model 'mock/rv' reviewed ambiguous cases (parsed 0 files, matched 0 columns, merged 0 labels)."
        ]
